      "body": "## Failure\nThe repository-wide `extractions/setup-just` installer fails intermittently with `no release for just matching version specifier` even after upgrading to v4 and pinning `1.58.0`. PR #2213 Quality re-run reproduced the failure after #2228 independently succeeded, demonstrating non-determinism in upstream release discovery.\n\n## Fix\nIntroduce one local composite action `.github/actions/setup-just/action.yml` that downloads the exact official `just 1.58.0` Linux archive by immutable release URL for amd64/arm64, verifies its official SHA-256 digest, and installs it on `GITHUB_PATH`. No GitHub Release API/semver enumeration, no `curl | sh`, bounded retries, and explicit unknown-architecture failure.\n\nChange only `.github/workflows/ci-quality.yml` Rust/Web jobs to use the local action. Tests and Gates stay unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n- [#2228 successful initial setup and Quality](https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/actions/runs/39817672179).\n- [#2213 failure after pinned v4](https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/actions/runs/39818271966).\n- Verify the local action via a full Quality run; successful SHA check and `just --version` must precede actual Rust/Web Gates.\n- The source `casey/just` release `1.58.0` asset digests are pinned in the action.\n\nA main-only workflow/tooling fix, independent of ACR image build. Once proven, sync the same installer into #2213's staging/production release workflows and #2226's staging branch. Merge with merge commit only."
