      "url": "https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/pull/2518",
      "body": "## Outcome\n\nReplace the original 15-minute prototype polling proposal with an **event-driven, least-privilege workflow bridge**.\n\n- **Producer (already on orphan `prototype` branch):** `.github/workflows/prototype-changed.yml`, display name `Prototype / Change Signal`, runs on `push: prototype`. Only `contents: read` permission, no checkout of prototype assets, no secrets, no privileged dispatch. [Verified first successful push Run #40484537507](https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/actions/runs/40484537507), source commit `dd5e84cd...`.\n- **Consumer (`main`, this PR):** `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` listens to `workflow_run: completed` scoped to `Prototype / Change Signal` on the `prototype` branch. The build job requires successful, same-repository, prototype-branch, **push** upstream. It executes only the trusted `main` sanitizer and Pages publisher; no upstream artifacts/code are executed or privileged tokens passed to the signal.\n- Keep existing main push, 4-hour scheduled public metrics refresh, and manual dispatch unchanged. **Remove the 15-minute polling implementation and tests completely.**\n- Update `nession-prototype` Skill and `pages/README.md` for the single audited signal-only orphan workflow exception, and add source-aligned test cases.\n- **Workflow audit:** The canonical main-owned workflow taxonomy/trigger-inventory now recognizes this exact cross-branch producer **only** for the named `deploy-pages.yml` consumer with explicit event/branch/conclusion/repository restrictions. Other unregistered `workflow_run` sources still fail closed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Unprivileged prototype signal actually executed from a real orphan branch push: [Run 40484537507](https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/actions/runs/40484537507) **success**.\n- `CI / Pages` passed on earlier PR revision; `CI / Quality Gate` identified an unregistered upstream. This PR fixes the validator rather than skipping the Gate, and new CI must pass on final exact HEAD.\n- On merge: check that `Deploy / Public Pages` consumes a **new** signal run (a producer run from before the workflow was merged will not be retroactively replayed). Confirm HTTPS `prototypes/manifest.json` includes `agent-process-discovery-2514` and that its HTML serves publicly.\n- Caveat: updates committed by other GitHub Actions using their default `GITHUB_TOKEN` may not emit another workflow run due to GitHub recursion prevention. Approved GitHub App/personal pushes do emit source events; don't promise universal triggering in unsupported writer paths.\n\nRefs: #2519\n\nContext: prototype #2514 first exposed stale Pages publication, but this infrastructure PR does not implement Session process discovery. Workflow-only direct-to-main PR per `.github/AGENTS.md`; merge commits only (`--merge`)."
