      "title": "fix(agent): apply a created Session's size against client sizing (#2520)",
      "author": "BestNathan",
      "updated": "2026-10-27T15:15:21Z",
      "created": "2026-10-27T13:03:50Z",
      "state": "merged",
      "draft": false,
      "head": "fix/2520-standalone-width",
      "headRepo": "BestNathan/nession",
      "base": "staging",
      "changedFiles": 17,
      "additions": 934,
      "deletions": 22,
      "commits": 9,
      "url": "https://github.com/BestNathan/nession/pull/2522",
      "body": "Refs #2520\nRefs #2487\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe new create-time diagnostics identified the event on the CI runner's tmux 3.4: the target Session was **never** 96. With the default `window-size latest`, a client attached to another Session at 80×24 sized the **newly created** Session to 80×24, discarding `new-session -x 96 -y 24`; the create response returned that pane. Evidence from run `40512783428`:\n\n```\nafter_create=[ids=$30 @30 %30 window=80x24 pane=80x24 attached=0\n              window-size= default-size=80x24 global-window-size=latest\n              clients=/dev/pts/21 nession-test-width-anchor-... 80x24\n              server=19729 /tmp/nession-test-tmux.../tmux.sock]\n```\n\nThis is a product defect on a shared Agent tmux server, not test-only interference: the production-equivalent multi-Session test failed the same way. It is also a violation of #2487's SC-09 invariant (“a real Agent created a new Session at the configured width”), which held only on an otherwise quiet server at `ea22b038`.\n\n## Fix\n\n`create_session_impl` applies the requested geometry with `resize-window` after `new-session`. `resize-window` pins `window-size=manual` as a side effect, so the dynamic policy is restored best-effort (with a warning); the active controller's authorized resize path still drives rows. A regression witness, `a_client_attached_elsewhere_cannot_size_a_new_session`, holds a real 80×24 client on an anchor Session while creating a 96-column Session.\n\n## Reopening the #2487 SC-09 criterion\n\n#2520 SC-03 requires a real product defect to reopen #2487 SC-09 with a distinct live witness rather than close it as test-only isolation. This PR adds that witness to `e2e/acceptance/cases/2487/SC-09` (the same regression test, run by its Case on the real server), corrects SC-03's verdict — it had said “no product regression is proven”, which the finding makes false — and records the determination in the isolation doc. After this merges, #2487 is reopened at SC-09, its Case runs at the new staging SHA, and only then is it re-accepted and closed again; the old `ea22b038` receipt is preserved in its report.\n\n## Also in this PR\n\n- Four-point diagnostics in the standalone width test (Session/Window/Pane ids, `window-size`, `default-size`, clients, server identity) — these produced the root cause.\n- `configured_width_survives_shared_server_flood_and_attach` (SC-02) and `shared_agent_keeps_independent_session_widths` (SC-03) as the explicit schedules.\n- Coverage-gate reporting (SC-05): a failed test run is no longer reported as “cargo llvm-cov not installed”; the selftest injects both signatures and is wired into the Rust Quality suite through `detector-selftest-coverage`.\n- `docs/architecture/agent-tmux-test-isolation.md` (tmux-version matrix, diagnosis, audit) and the sizing-doctrine note.\n- `e2e/acceptance/cases/2520/SC-02|SC-03|SC-05`; the Issue plan moved those three to merged-staging Cases (a `when: pr` + Case criterion cannot project a Pass). SC-01/SC-04 remain PR-head Agent evaluations, and both Pass at `1be09f302` (run `40520245382`).\n\n## Verification\n\n- Pre-push gates: `dev-workspace-push`, `rust-test-unit`, `rust-test-integration`, `rust-coverage`, `design-system-full`.\n- Full integration suite 92/92 locally; the standalone, multi-Session and flood+client width tests pass.\n- `check-coverage-selftest.sh` 6/6; `detector-selftest-coverage` passes.\n- `acceptance-cases-contract`, `acceptance-layout-contract`, `acceptance-runtime-contract` pass with the edited Cases; the #2487 SC-09 reopen witness runs green under `cargo test -p nession-agent --lib -- --exact`.\n- The CI Linux/tmux-3.4 run is the authority for the regression witness.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n"
